(PRC-50 — any reap form takes a `without waiting` suffix (WNOHANG).
 Also covers: PRC-51 (a finished child -> its PID, flag cleared), PRC-52
 (children exist but none finished -> 0, flag cleared, NOT an error),
 PRC-53 (genuine error -> negative, flag set) and PRC-54 (a poll that
 returns 0 reaps nothing, so it does not disturb `the reaped status`,
 which is still the -1 sentinel here).
 SAFETY: signal 9 goes only to the pid this program forked.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-50.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   polling a running child returned 0
   the reaped status is still -1
   the killed child was reaped
   its terminating signal was 9
   polling with no children left set the error flag
   it returned -10
)
a number called 'the slow child' is fork the process.
If 'the slow child' is 0 then, Wait 2 seconds, Exit 0.
a number called 'the poll while running' is reap any child process without waiting.
On error print "polling a running child set the error flag".
print "polling a running child returned {'the poll while running'}".
print "the reaped status is still {the reaped status}".
Send signal 9 to process 'the slow child'.
a number called 'the blocking reap' is reap child 'the slow child'.
If 'the blocking reap' is 'the slow child' then, print "the killed child was reaped".
print "its terminating signal was {the reaped status bit-and 127}".
a number called 'the poll with no children' is reap any child process without waiting.
On error print "polling with no children left set the error flag".
print "it returned {'the poll with no children'}".
